{"baselines":{"inline":"rocksdb","separated":"rocksdb_blob"},"groups":[{"name":"write_throughput","note":"Bulk insert of N fresh keys into an empty engine, then one flush. Covers open, memtable inserts and the flush that writes the table. Both engines compress blocks on 4 threads."},{"name":"overwrite","note":"Every key written a second time into an engine that already holds one copy, then one flush. Memtable churn over existing keys and a superseding flush. Both engines compress blocks on 4 threads. ours-deferred-wal: our engine with a caller-kept log, the log written and synced once and the flush deferred, one sync per batch as in SurrealKV's commit."},{"name":"overwrite_sustained","note":"100,000 keys, then 15 rewrites of a hot set of 20,000 of them, with compaction behind the writes and a reader alongside. 4 MiB memtables, 2 MiB tables, 4 L0 runs per compaction, no write-ahead log on either. Ours flushes on a thread of its own as RocksDB does, one sealed memtable at a time as RocksDB's two write buffers allow, with deferred durability and one sync barrier per 8 flushes; it runs leveled compaction on another thread and stops writes at 36 L0 runs, RocksDB's stop trigger. Time per write; beside it the compaction bytes per written byte until compaction rests, the disk bytes over live bytes when the last write lands, and the reader's p50 and p99."},{"name":"point_read","note":"One get per stored key on a warm engine. Also our hash index, ribbon locator and row cache, and RocksDB's hash index, on the same chart."},{"name":"multi_get","note":"One batched lookup of the whole key set on a warm engine (RocksDB: batched_multi_get_cf)."},{"name":"range_scan","note":"A full forward scan reading every value on a warm engine."},{"name":"seek_random","note":"A seek to each key in scattered order, reading the value under the cursor."},{"name":"major_compact_zstd3","note":"Six overlapping L0 tables merged into one level, 4-thread block compression, no range split. zstd level 3, the level RocksDB applies to bottommost output."},{"name":"subcompaction_zstd3","note":"A full overwrite in six L0 tables merged into a bottom level of several tables, split into 4 parallel ranges. High-entropy values. zstd level 3."}],"preset":"rocksdb-parity","results":[{"engine":"ours","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":1000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":2286.024,"median":2344.927833333333,"upper":2456.9265555555558},"rounds":30,"values":"inline","vs_baseline":{"lower":0.1425091672339589,"median":0.14485053621187743,"upper":0.14882990612113636}},{"engine":"rocksdb","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":1000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":15957.536000000002,"median":16229.11625,"upper":16550.9745},"rounds":30,"values":"inline","vs_baseline":null},{"engine":"surrealkv","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":1000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":4757.089,"median":4875.1033333333335,"upper":4956.668333333333},"rounds":30,"values":"inline","vs_baseline":{"lower":0.2913345398170816,"median":0.29801123214158276,"upper":0.3052294296920775}},{"engine":"blob_tree","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":1000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":2781.826625,"median":2901.3655,"upper":2964.815125},"rounds":30,"values":"separated","vs_baseline":{"lower":0.15628247721556884,"median":0.161521795451401,"upper":0.16721376660623663}},{"engine":"rocksdb_blob","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":1000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":17507.565,"median":17867.9215,"upper":18211.3075},"rounds":30,"values":"separated","vs_baseline":null},{"engine":"ours","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":10000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":1663.5097000000003,"median":1689.0264,"upper":1729.0947},"rounds":25,"values":"inline","vs_baseline":{"lower":0.4625095394392392,"median":0.4722150921767896,"upper":0.48181375827311546}},{"engine":"rocksdb","group":"write_throughput","metrics":[],"n":10000,"ns_per_op":{"lower":3507.4999,"median":3580.2681,"upper":3696.3384},"rounds":25,"values":"inline","vs_baseline":null},{"engine":"surrealkv"